---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="How Viger Cloud uses cookies and similar technologies."
>
  <section class="section container legal-content">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: July 2026</p>

    <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help sites
      remember preferences and understand how visitors use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies we use</h2>

    <h3>Strictly necessary</h3>
    <p>
      Required for authentication and security. These include Clerk session cookies when you sign
      in to the app portal or Viger Cloud applications. These cannot be disabled while using
      signed-in features.
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics (optional)</h3>
    <p>
      If enabled, we use privacy-friendly analytics (Plausible) to understand page views and
      referral sources. Plausible does not use cookies by default and does not track individuals
      across sites. No personal data is sold to advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can control cookies through your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies
      will prevent sign-in from working correctly.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Clerk (authentication) may set cookies when you sign in. See Clerk's privacy documentation
      for details. We do not use third-party advertising cookies on viger.cloud.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@viger.cloud">privacy@viger.cloud</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
